      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just updated my A records for a client site but the new IP isnt showing up for me yet. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually work everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It can take anywhere from 15 minutes to 96 hours for DNS changes to propagate globally. The time frame is due to the spread of DNS changes across the internet's large network of Domain Name Servers (DNS providers). It also depends on the type of change, with priority updates (like A records) typically taking around 48 hours to propagate globally. This allows any cached DNS entries to expire and be re-populated with the new IP address.",
