    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "does it have anything to do with TTL? i noticed the TTL was set pretty high on the old record, could that be the main cause for the delay?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, the Time to Live (TTL) setting can indeed impact the propagation time. If the TTL is set high, it allows the old IP address to remain cached for a longer period, delaying when the new IP address is actually propagated to the internet. A lower TTL would speed up the propagation process, but it also increases the risk of the unchanged record being returned if the new record is not yet cached.",
      "source": "target",
